        <dc:title>Cloud Container Technologies in Military Applications</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Cloud container technologies have rapidly emerged as a cornerstone of modern software deployment and management, offering agility, scalability, and resilience. Militaries around the world are exploring and adopting these technologies to modernize systems and enhance operational capabilities. This paper presents a comprehensive review of cloud container technologies in military applications from a practical, application-oriented perspective. We discuss the fundamentals of containerization and orchestration, their advantages for defense systems, and the current state of adoption in the United States Department of Defense (DoD) including initiatives like DevSecOps and examples such as the Advanced Battle Management System (ABMS), U-2 Dragon Lady, F-16 fighter, and MQ-20 Avenger unmanned aircraft. We also examine efforts by other nations and alliances (NATO, UK, France, etc.) to leverage cloud-native architectures for defense. We address the benefits in development speed, system agility, and security hardening, as well as challenges such as security risks and integration complexity. Looking ahead, we outline emerging trends including multi-cloud and hybrid cloud deployments, integration of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning at the tactical edge, and the role of cloud containers in future command-andcontrol and combat systems.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2025-07</dc:date>
        <z:libraryCatalog>IEEE Xplore</z:libraryCatalog>
